From: jayweihung <3034830+jayweihung@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 00:07:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 34/34] feat: programs.json check: an agent started through a
 launcher (run: kit open claude ...) counts as installed when check is, not
 run's first word

knownAgents() gives each agent its check (default: run's first word) and judges installed by it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 defaults/AGENTS.md  |  7 +++++--
 defaults/herdr.d.ts |  2 +-
 src/mods.rs         | 14 +++++++++++---
 src/programs.rs     | 26 +++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 4 files changed, 42 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/defaults/AGENTS.md b/defaults/AGENTS.md
index 5a2af9f..84db73f 100644
--- a/defaults/AGENTS.md
+++ b/defaults/AGENTS.md
@@ -916,7 +916,10 @@ has 124 programs (agents, editors, runtimes, tools, databases, infra);
   `"claude": { "run": ["my-claude"] }` or add
   `"claude-alt": { "name": "Claude (alt)", "icon": "icons/claude.svg", "run": ["my-claude-alt"] }`
   inside `programs`. Use programs or shell functions, not aliases (the launcher
-  does not expand them). On macOS both checks and the menu launcher load login profiles before
+  does not expand them). `check`: the program that must be there for it to
+  count as installed, when `run` starts it through a launcher, for example
+  `"claude": { "run": ["kit", "open", "claude", "--tab-env", "HC_TERMINAL_ID", "--"], "check": "claude" }`
+  (default: `run`'s first word). On macOS both checks and the menu launcher load login profiles before
   running the agent and leaves an interactive login shell when it ends.
   Codex starts as `codex --no-daemon`: a shared Codex daemon would make later
   sessions use the first terminal's identity and stop with it.
@@ -1289,7 +1292,7 @@ All of it is in `herdr.d.ts`. In short:
   `hc(args)` (`hc read <t>` gives a terminal's text),
   `home()`, `appHome()`, `playSound("done" | "blocked" | file)`.
   `knownAgents({ on })`: the agents people can start (programs.json's
-  `run`), most picked first, each `installed` or not there (asked of the
+  `run`), most picked first, each `installed` or not there (judged by `check`) (asked of the
   shell agents start in; a remote Unix machine's login/interactive shell when supported);
   rejects if the check fails (failed checks are not cached); start one with `argv: agent.run`.
   `pickFolder({ prompt })`: the system's folder picker (here only),
